

## 🚀 Getting started (WSL, no Docker)

This is the WSL-native equivalent of `cp .env.example .env && docker
compose up -d` — no Docker involved. Run all of this from a WSL2 Ubuntu
terminal, inside the project folder. (Airflow doesn't run natively on
Windows — WSL is the Linux environment it needs.)

### Prerequisites — one-time
```bash
mkdir -p dags include sql scripts tests
```

copy requirements.txt into the folder

Airflow 2.9.3 doesn't support very new Python releases (no published
constraints file, and some dependency wheels won't build). Pin to Python
3.11 explicitly rather than trusting whatever `python3` defaults to on a
fresh WSL image — check first:

```bash
python3 --version
```

If that's not 3.11.x, install 3.11 alongside it (this does not remove or
touch your default `python3`):

```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y python3.11 python3.11-venv
```

If apt reports "unable to locate package python3.11" (can happen on a
very new Ubuntu release that's dropped it from the default repos), add
the deadsnakes PPA first, then retry the line above:

